<title>USA: TABLE - Capitol Multimedia Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Capitol Multimedia Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>CONCORD, Mass. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pro Forma</p>
<p>		     Quarter Ended June 30  Quarter Ended June 30</p>
<p>			     1997	 1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net Sales	 $   918,969$ 1,012,549$   918,969$ 1,303,642</p>
<p>Gain on Sale of</p>
<p>  Assets	     2,037,104	   --	   --	   --</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)</p>
<p>			 1,673,712     81,740  (203,844)    136,168</p>
<p> EPS			  0.26	 0.02     (0.03)	 0.02</p>
<p>Weighted Average</p>
<p>Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding	6,914,348  4,832,065  6,032,065  6,032,065</p>
<p>NOTE:  Capitol Multimedia Inc said its first quarter period ended June 30.</p>
<p>The proforma results assume the acquisition of Client Server Technologies Inc and sale of selected multimedia assets occurred prior to April 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Net income for the first quarter includes a gain of $2.0 million associated with the sale of selected multimedia assets to Davidson &amp; Associates Inc in April 1997.</p>
<p>The company said that almost all of the revenue in the first quarter of 1997 was generated by Davidson.</p>
